---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import type { Locale } from '../../i18n/config';
import { t } from '../../i18n/t';

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}

const { locale } = Astro.props;
const description =
  'What JSON Bits stores, what it never sees, and why every tool works without sending your JSON anywhere. A plain summary of local processing.';
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  title={t(locale, 'privacy.metaTitle')}
  description={description}
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-20 pt-10 sm:px-6 sm:pt-14">
    <h1 class="text-[32px] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[44px]">
      {t(locale, 'privacy.title')}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[26px] text-body">{t(locale, 'privacy.description')}</p>

    <div class="md-body mt-8">
      <p>
        JSON Bits is built so that your documents have nowhere to go. Every tool on this site runs
        inside the browser tab you already have open. There is no upload step, no account, and no
        server that receives the JSON you paste or open.
      </p>

      <h2>Your JSON stays in the tab</h2>
      <p>
        Formatting, validation, conversion, comparison, and repair all run in a Web Worker created
        by the page. The worker is part of the same browser tab. Data you paste, drop, or open with
        the file picker is read locally with the browser's File API and processed in memory.
      </p>
      <p>
        The document is never written to storage, never included in a cookie, and never attached to
        an analytics event. When you close or reload the tab, it is gone.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
      <p>Two preferences are kept in <code>localStorage</code> so the site remembers them:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The theme you picked: light or dark.</li>
        <li>The indent size you last chose for formatting.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Those values contain no document content. Clearing site data in your browser removes them,
        and the site falls back to its defaults.
      </p>

      <h2>Network requests</h2>
      <p>
        The page loads only its own static files: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, the self-hosted Inter font,
        and the favicon. There are no third-party scripts, no analytics, no advertising pixels, and
        no external fonts or CDNs.
      </p>
      <p>
        A Content Security Policy sent with every page sets <code>connect-src 'none'</code>, which
        stops the page from making <code>fetch</code>, XHR, or WebSocket requests. That rule is a
        technical guarantee, not only a promise.
      </p>
      <p>
        Like any website, the host that delivers these files (Cloudflare Pages) receives standard
        request metadata such as your IP address, browser version, and the page you requested. That
        is ordinary web hosting. It does not include the content you paste into a tool.
      </p>

      <h2>Files and downloads</h2>
      <p>
        Opening a file reads it locally. Downloading a result creates a temporary
        <code>Blob</code> URL inside the tab, which the browser revokes after the download starts.
        No file is uploaded to create it.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        There are no ads on the site today. If non-intrusive ads are added later, they will be clearly
        marked, will never sit above or inside a tool, and will not read the content of your
        documents. This page will be updated before any advertising is enabled.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If the way the site handles data changes, this page changes with it. The date below records
        the last revision.
      </p>
      <p>
        <time datetime="2026-11-11">Last updated 11 November 2026</time>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
